      {
        "id": "source-section-contact-and-entry",
        "description": "Right: horizontal shaft crosses the housing and extends beyond both sides; its right end has the source's stepped outline and a short collar boundary. Upper and lower thin bushing strips lie between the shaft and upper/lower housing. The shaft top meets the inner upper bushing boundary and the shaft bottom meets the inner lower boundary: no visible air gap and no shaft passing through housing material. The upper housing has a sloping roof and the lower block meets a long support baseline. Component 4 is a short fitted oil inlet at the top, above the bushing, with its visible lower end entering the upper housing. The source does not expose the complete hidden oil passage; do not invent that passage, flow arrows, or a lubrication measurement. Unlabelled boundary anchors and exact parallelism are modern executable regularization of these observed relationships.",
